{
	// Lint runs in CI and gates on errors only, so oxlint's exit code blocks new
	// violations without the pre-existing warning debt blocking this branch. There
	// is deliberately no warning-count threshold: the counter would need updating
	// on every change and would gate on a number rather than on a rule.
	//
	// No source file is edited to satisfy the linter, and there are no inline
	// suppressions. The reasoning lives here instead, one entry per group.
	//
	// Debt — clears as behaviour fixes land, since each fix rewrites a runtime
	// expression. There is no single "behaviour PR": each pinned bug is one issue
	// and one PR, so this debt clears a piece at a time and most PRs clear none.
	//
	//   no-unused-expressions          7  lib/api/api.ts, lib/drivers/ddp.ts
	//   no-this-alias                  2  lib/api/RocketChat.ts
	//
	//     No issue owns these nine. They are not pinned bugs, so nothing on the
	//     tracker will clear them as a side effect — they need their own change.
	//
	// Live defect — not merely cosmetic, and owned:
	//
	//   no-async-promise-executor      1  lib/drivers/ddp.ts, the send path.
	//     A bare `throw` sits inside an async executor, so it rejects the
	//     executor's own promise instead of settling the outer one. Callers
	//     awaiting a send on a closed connection hang forever.
	//     Fixed by issue #203, which pins the hang.
	//
	// Not debt — correct as written, do not "fix":
	//
	//   no-this-alias                  1  lib/util.ts, the debounce helper.
	//     NEVER FIX. The alias forwards the *caller's* `this` into the deferred
	//     call. An arrow function would capture the wrong one.
	//
	//   triple-slash-reference         1  lib/drivers/ddp.ts
	//     NEVER FIX. It points at an ambient module declaration, and ambient
	//     modules are not importable. It is also the only thing pulling that
	//     declaration into the *app's* compile — the app's config will never glob
	//     this repo's declaration directory. Deleting it breaks the app with an
	//     implicit-any error that this repo's CI cannot observe.
	//
	//   no-unsafe-declaration-merging  1  lib/message.ts
	//     A documented workaround for a long-standing TypeScript issue.
	//
	//   no-async-promise-executor      1  lib/drivers/ddp.ts, the open path.
	//     Benign: the body is fully wrapped and both paths settle.
	//
	//   no-unused-vars                 3  lib/clients/Livechat.ts
	//     Destructured constructor parameters that exist to strip keys out of
	//     `...config`. The `_` convention cannot apply: renaming one changes which
	//     property is stripped.
	//
	// Total: 17 warnings, 0 errors.
	//
	// Every warning above is shipped-source debt. Specs and test helpers lint under
	// these same rules — there are no test-file overrides and no rule changes for
	// them — and test code stays at zero warnings. So the count above is also the
	// budget: if it grows, the growth came from test code and is a real regression.
	//
	// Every rule below carries violations, so none can be promoted to error yet.
	// A rule reaches "error" once its entry above is cleared.
	"rules": {
		"no-unused-expressions": "warn",
		"no-this-alias": "warn",
		"no-async-promise-executor": "warn",
		"triple-slash-reference": "warn",
		"no-unsafe-declaration-merging": "warn",
		"no-unused-vars": "warn"
	}
}
